# Shabakat

Flutter ISP/management app. Clean Architecture. Dart ^3.11.5, Riverpod (`riverpod_generator`), Dio, Freezed, Json Serializable.

## Architecture

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Domain | `lib/domain/` | Entities, repository contracts. No implementation deps. |
| Data | `lib/data/` | Repository implementations, providers, remote/local sources. |
| Core | `lib/core/` | Network, enums, themes, utilities. |
| UI | `lib/ui/` | Presentation. Riverpod for state. |
| Infrastructor | `lib/infrastructor/` | DB, migrations, seed data. |

Work step by step (DTO → entity → mapper → UI) only when told. Smallest correct diff. Do not run codegen unless asked.

## Commands

```bash
flutter pub get
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
flutter run
flutter test
```

Use `freezed` for models, `riverpod_generator` for providers. No `print()` — use `logger` or `debugPrint()`. Generated `*.g.dart` / `*.freezed.dart` are excluded from analysis.

## Simple Logic — No Overengineering

### Providers

State holders only. No screen-specific or field-specific methods.

- `build()` → empty/default instance
- One generic update that merges state (`copyWith` or assign)
- One clear/reset method
- UI reads current state, runs its own logic, passes the result to update

```dart
// ❌ BAD
void updateSearch(...) { ... }
void updateArea(...) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
void update(StateModel next) {
  state = state.copyWith(/* fields from next */);
}
void clear() => state = const StateModel();
```

```dart
final current = ref.read(provider);
ref.read(provider.notifier).update(
  current.copyWith(/* only what this screen changed */),
);
```

### Riverpod docs (Context7)

When the user says `use context7` for Riverpod — or asks about `riverpod`, `flutter_riverpod`, or `riverpod_generator` APIs — fetch current docs via CLI before answering:

```bash
npx ctx7@latest library riverpod "<specific question>"
npx ctx7@latest docs <libraryId> "<specific question>"
```

If `riverpod` is ambiguous, also try `flutter_riverpod` or `riverpod_generator`. Use the library ID from step 1 (format `/org/project`). Do not use Context7 for Shabakat business logic or project-specific provider code unless the user asks.


One file, one screen widget. Private helpers/widgets stay in that file.

- No external callbacks to wire behavior
- Watch provider for data and loading
- Local draft vs original — submit disabled until they differ
- Loading: dim content + centered spinner from provider `isLoading`
- Submit: `try/catch` → user feedback → `pop()` on success
- Change only what was asked; do not touch unrelated files

## Theming

Single source of truth under `lib/core/themes/`:

- Colors → `AppColors`. Gradients → `AppGradients` (from `AppColors` only).
- Component themes → `ControlsThemes` static factories.
- `ThemeSelector` is the only place that assembles `ThemeData`.

In widgets:

- Colors/styles from `Theme.of(context)` / `ColorScheme` — never `Colors.xxx`, never `isDarkMode` booleans.
- Text from `textTheme`; one-off tweaks via `.copyWith()`.
- Material widgets inherit theme by default — do not set `style`, `decoration`, `shape`, `backgroundColor`, or `foregroundColor` on instances unless overriding from theme.
- One-off overrides: `theme.<property>.copyWith(...)` — never a standalone style from scratch.
- New widget types: add theme to `ControlsThemes` first, register in `ThemeSelector`.

```dart
final theme = Theme.of(context);
TextField(
  decoration: theme.inputDecorationTheme.copyWith(
    hintText: 'Search...',
    prefixIcon: Icon(Icons.search, color: theme.colorScheme.outline),
  ),
);
```

## Layout

- Spacing, padding, breakpoints → `AppSizes` on `BuildContext` (`context.paddingMedium`, `context.borderRadiusLarge`, etc.). No magic numbers in widgets.
- Split large widgets into private classes (`_Header`, `_ActionButton`) instead of deep nesting.
- `const` constructors where possible. No comments unless logic is non-obvious.

## New UI checklist

1. Theme exists in `ControlsThemes`? → use via `ThemeSelector`.
2. Missing? → add to `ControlsThemes`, register in `ThemeSelector`.
3. Instance tweak? → `Theme.of(context).<property>.copyWith(...)`.
4. Never hardcode colors, shapes, or padding in build methods.
